    ('b', "**A precipitating event: hepatic (alcohol, hepatitis B flare) or extrahepatic (infection, GI bleed).** In the European cohorts bacterial infection and alcoholic hepatitis are the commonest single triggers; in about a third of patients no trigger is found, which does not exclude the diagnosis."),
